Modifications made in ProkBot Plus (2026-11-07 to 2026-11-24)
--------------------------------------------------------------

1. Windows x64 client (new)
   - windows/: patcher, recipes, per-user installer source (Go), prebuilt
     grokbot-tailcat.exe and installer stub, tests. The patcher builds from
     the official Windows 1.2.3 installer by default and from 1.1.0 / 0.71.2
     as fallbacks; inputs.mjs recognizes an input by size and SHA-256.
   - windows/tools/desktop-recipes/: generator, anchored edit list and the
     project code appended to original modules, producing the 1.2.3 recipes
     for Windows x64, macOS ARM64, macOS Intel, Linux x64 and Linux ARM64
     from the user's own original package. The 1.1.0 recipes come from the
     same tool at commit 8c1fcd1; the 0.71.2 recipes were ported from the
     earlier macOS 0.71.2 recipes.
   - windows/patchers/desktop/original.mjs: extraction of the official
     installer, shared with the Android and web client builders.
   - The installer tracks the files it owns, supports side-by-side migration
     of legacy installs and preserves occupied Start menu and URL entries.

2. Shared desktop client (mac/clients/desktop/)
   - Cross-platform changes shared by the macOS, Windows and Linux clients:
     platform.mjs, main.mjs, connection.mjs, settings.mjs, sounds.mjs,
     connect.css, native-provider.mjs, codex-bridge.mjs, codex-process.mjs,
     local-exec.mjs (UTF-8 command output on Windows, linux- machine ID on
     Linux) and attachments.mjs (POSIX Host image paths).
   - The 1.1.0 interfaces: per-edge RPC registration and window visibility
     events (main.mjs, local-services.mjs), dictation through the Host
     (dictation.mjs), search mapping (gateway.mjs) and startup defaults.
   - Connection lifecycle and reconnect fixes; on HTTP 401 the client checks
     /connect/status before disconnecting (gateway.mjs); settings survive
     failed saves and a damaged profile is kept under another name
     (client-persistence.mjs); the saved theme applies before first paint.
   - workspace.css and workspace-keys.cjs: wide reply tables, dialog send
     shortcuts and empty catalog-search dismissal, shared with Android.
   - host/runtime/host-computers.mjs, native-desktop.mjs, codex-prompt.mjs and
     host/server/desktop-capabilities.mjs: the Host recognizes Windows and
     Linux computers and withholds desktop execution from phones and browsers.
   - Intel macOS: mac/patchers/desktop/x64/ pins the official Intel build;
     patch.mjs picks the build for the Mac's chip, native-helper.mjs accepts
     the Intel copy of the computer helper, and
     mac/dist/network/x64/grokbot-tailcat is built by
     host/network/build-tailcat.py --target darwin-amd64.

3. Android client (new)
   - android/shell/: Android shell app (Kotlin, no third-party libraries):
     loopback gateway to the paired Host, Keystore-encrypted credential,
     pairing, background notifications, file picking and saving, back gesture.
     android/dist/grokbot-android-shell.apk is its prebuilt release build.
   - android/client/: bridge that runs the original desktop interface in the
     Android WebView in place of Electron's main process and preloads, the
     computer view frame with fresh tickets, a phone layout after the official
     phone app, an anchor positioning fallback, compatibility functions for
     older WebView builds (compat.js) and the connection page.
   - android/patchers/: builds the APK from the user's own official Windows
     installer (1.1.0 by default, 0.71.2 as a fallback), signs it with
     APK Signature Scheme v2 using a key created for the user, and applies a
     few verified changes to the original interface (renderer-patches.mjs).

4. Web client (new)
   - web/patchers/: builds a web client bundle from the user's own official
     Windows installer with the Windows recipes and the Android interface
     patches (patch.mjs), and installs it on the user's own Host through the
     admin API (upload.mjs). The bundle is never committed or published.
   - web/client/: browser start-up data, the browser stand-in for the Android
     shell's native calls, back navigation, keyboard, theme and notification
     handling, and browser styles.
   - host/server/web-client.mjs (new) and changes to index.mjs, auth.mjs,
     proxy.mjs and push-service.mjs: bundle verification, atomic install,
     serving only to signed-in browsers, the web device platform, cookie
     sign-in bound to the Host origin and a request header, admin routes, and
     the computer view bridge injected into noVNC pages. host/server/public/:
     sign-in page (web-login.*) and the admin Web client page (web-client.js).
   - android/client/: a Safari ResizeObserver shim (compat.js) and deep links
     that wait for the Bot list (bridge.js), shared with Android.

5. Model API formats and routing
   - New Anthropic Messages and OpenAI Responses adapters next to OpenAI Chat:
     host/runtime/anthropic-messages.mjs, openai-responses.mjs,
     openai-chat.mjs, model-common.mjs (new); model-session.mjs,
     model-policy.mjs, model-router.mjs, model-errors.mjs,
     model-observation.mjs, config.mjs, host/server/models.mjs, index.mjs,
     public/model.js, public/locales-en.js and public/ids.js (changed or new).
   - "minimal" reasoning effort, reasoning provenance tags, optional-parameter
     fallback, bounded error bodies, incremental SSE parsing, connection tests
     and auto review for all three formats. OpenAI Chat accepts either
     completion marker and tool calls after "stop"; empty tool arguments mean
     {} only for tools without required parameters. Malformed function calls
     are omitted from replay and rejected before they are persisted.
   - Per-Bot model routes and profiles with ordered fallbacks
     (host/runtime/model-routing.mjs, contributed through pull request #2),
     the rewritten model page, guarded manual summarization
     (host-summarize.mjs), threshold compaction and rejection of malformed
     provider function names (model-rejection-guard.mjs).

6. Auto review, web and image tools
   - Auto review retries once on a malformed classification and logs failures
     (host/runtime/host-auto-review.mjs).
   - Native web tools fall back to automatic tool choice when a model rejects a
     forced tool call; parallel searches succeed when one call succeeds
     (host/runtime/web-services.mjs).
   - Aspect ratios are mapped to image sizes, and reference images use the
     image edits endpoint (host/server/media-providers.mjs, media-http.mjs,
     media-settings.mjs, host/runtime/media-services.mjs).

7. Message order and reliability
   - Messages from one model response are delivered in the order the model
     wrote them; IDs reused by concurrent responses run unordered
     (host/runtime/reliability/tool-order.mjs (new), tool-journal.mjs).
   - An immediate resend of an acknowledged plain-text delivery stops before
     another send. A failed post-turn memory request no longer stops the Host.
   - The Host patch build verifies each prepared reliability file against its
     protected manifest; the Harness turn-run recipe passes the Bot ID to the
     main and summarization sessions.

8. Linux deployment, ARM64, backup and recovery
   - host/deploy.py and host/release/: one operator entry point for checks,
     setup, start, update, backup and recovery; build before stopping
     services; validated Compose mounts; exact-image recovery into new volumes
     (backup.py), including Docker 29 with Compose 2.40.
   - ARM64 Host build path, locked ARM runtime dependencies
     (host/release/arm-runtime/), ARM64 Tailcat and platform checks
     (platforms.py). The original desktop is unchanged and stays amd64.
   - build-docker.py accepts Docker 29's containerd image identities;
     host/network/build-tailcat.py builds the Windows target; the Dockerfiles
     set the executable bit on Tailcat; streamed, verified Host patch output.
   - host/bench/: whole-machine resource sampling and comparison.

9. Admin tools: host/tools/host-admin.mjs (new) and admin page status and
   CLI error handling.

10. Release engineering: ci/ (input checks, homepage version tables, official
    channel snapshots, release packaging and verification of nested ZIP, APK
    and gzip content, inactive workflow templates).

11. Tests: host/tests/, windows/tests/, linux/tests/, android/tests/,
    web/tests/ (new) and mac/tests/ additions.

12. Documentation: README, docs/AI-INSTALL, docs/ARCHITECTURE (also covering
    the upstream DETAILS.md, TODO.md and install notes, and the maintenance
    notes), module READMEs (host and ios also cover the upstream DEPLOYMENT,
    PLUGINS and SIGNING notes), AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY,
    GitHub issue and pull request templates, and demo screenshots. Unused
    files were removed (host/source-files.json, an unreferenced plugin
    example, an outdated Android browser test and old screenshots).

13. Host memory visibility in the execution desktop. host/release/compose.yaml
    mounts the five protected data trees agents, user-memory, workflows,
    plugins and managed-skills only below the protected
    /data/runtime/host-data root; agent-transcripts and other Host-only data
    stay out of Box. host/release/data_init.py changes ownership and mode only
    on directories it creates. host/release/backup.py validates exact mounts.
    host/runtime/prompt-runtime.mjs preserves proactive memory retrieval, adds
    its live-access reminder only for the local Box topology and falls back to
    the original prompt when the extra text exceeds the size limit. Same-machine
    deployment refuses Docker Engine below 26.0, API 1.45 or Compose 2.26.0
    before writing or starting a subpath-mount configuration; distribution
    version suffixes are accepted and --host-only is not gated. Contributed by
    @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #5). Clients are unchanged.

14. Per-Bot voices. host/server/voice-selection.mjs (new), voice-config.mjs,
    voice-synthesis.mjs, voice-session.mjs, voice.mjs and the admin voice page
    (public/voice.js, speech.js, locales-en.js) match each Bot's name, title
    and description against candidate voices on the Host, so every client
    shares them; existing configurations keep the feature off. Contributed by
    @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #10).

15. Desktop 1.2.3 (Windows x64, macOS ARM64 and macOS Intel).
    - windows/patchers/desktop/ pins the official 1.2.3 by default and keeps
      1.1.0 (windows/patchers/desktop/1.1.0/) and 0.71.2 as fallbacks, which
      Android and the web client continue to use.
    - mac/patchers/desktop/ and mac/patchers/desktop/x64/ pin the official
      1.2.3; native-helper.mjs accepts its universal CUGrokBotService helper.
    - mac/clients/desktop/gateway.mjs and local-services.mjs answer the RPCs
      1.2.3 adds; windows/tools/desktop-recipes/build.mjs builds all three
      targets and --check compares decompressed recipes.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #11).

16. Host compatibility and reliability.
    - host/server/client-compat-api.mjs (new) answers the RPCs newer clients
      forward to the Host that d0a4baa lacks: in-conversation search,
      rerunning an automation from its card, an empty skill publishing target
      list and an explicit failure for webhook runs. notifications.mjs replays
      retained notifications in bounded, backpressured writes; proxy.mjs
      waits up to 120 s for response headers.
    - host/runtime/recovered-blob-worker.mjs and recovered-modules.mjs open a
      large conversation-blobs.db with a structural probe and run quick_check
      in a background thread; a corrupted database goes through the original
      recovery on the next open. host/release/compose*.yaml pass
      GROKBOT_BLOB_DB_QUICK_CHECK_MAX_BYTES.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #9).

17. iOS 1.27.0.
    - ios/recipes/ios/ pins the official 1.27.0 (build 29519) and keeps 1.26.0
      (29388) and 1.16.0 (23152) as pinned fallbacks. ios/tools/hbc98/,
      build_ios_127_recipe.py and build_ios_126_recipe.py rebuild the bytecode
      recipes from the user's own app.
    - ios/patchers/ios/ checks extensions per release and writes only the App
      Groups a provisioning profile grants (extensions.py, signing.py,
      patch-app.py).
    - ios/clients/ios/ and ios/bin/GrokBotLocal.dylib: keychain credential
      sync, sign-out from Settings, a Connect to Host entry on the sign-in
      screen, NSURLSession protocol injection that keeps the app's own
      session configuration, local Auto-review preferences and Pages RPC
      forwarding. host/server/mobile-rpc-compat.mjs (new) answers the Pages
      and MCP tool permission RPCs.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #14).

18. Linux x64 / ARM64 desktop client (new).
    - linux/: patcher, pure-Node .deb (ar) parser and verifier (deb.mjs),
      recipes for 1.2.3 x64 and ARM64 generated by
      windows/tools/desktop-recipes/build.mjs, portable launcher and per-user
      install/uninstall/AppArmor scripts (launcher.mjs), tar.gz builder
      (tar.mjs) and tests, reusing the Linux Tailcat binaries in host/bin/.
      The install and uninstall scripts replace or remove only an empty
      directory or an earlier Grok Bot Local install.
    - mac/clients/desktop/: Linux window chrome, tray, keyring fallback,
      notification sounds, linux- machine IDs and Codex delegation.
      host/server/desktop-capabilities.mjs, push-service.mjs,
      public/devices.js and host/runtime/host-computers.mjs recognize Linux
      desktop clients. ci/release-packages.py builds a seventh, Linux package.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #16).

19. iOS injection library thermal, hot-path, and thread-safety hardening.
    - ios/clients/ios/ and ios/bin/GrokBotLocal.dylib: eliminated the 120Hz
      Fabric RCTRecursiveAccessibilityLabel addSubview/removeFromSuperview
      thrash loop on plugin buttons, added O(1) layoutSubviews fast-path
      short-circuiting and cached sets/classes, guarded frame/text/zPosition
      and bringSubviewToFront updates, restored hidden sibling paragraph views
      on recycle, limited GBObserveRequest JSON parsing to
      /api/openAgentWindowed, cached GBDiagnosticsEnabled() and privacy domain
      lists, added capped exponential backoff and O(N) SSE parsing in
      GBNotifications, made direct-mode GBNetwork checks lock-free and off the
      main thread, synchronized cross-thread credential/protocol state, and
      fixed voice socket/audio leaks, swizzle ordering, and KVO/NSNull/empty
      displayName crashes. Updated dylibSha256 across 1.27.0, 1.26.0, and
      1.16.0 manifests.
    - Contributed by @jun9100 (GitHub pull request #15).

Third-party components
----------------------

Third-party components keep their own licenses. See host/THIRD_PARTY,
mac/THIRD_PARTY, ios/THIRD_PARTY and mac/patchers/desktop/node_modules.
ios/tools/hbc98/opcodes-v98.json derives its Hermes bytecode v98 opcode table
from Meta's facebook/hermes (include/hermes/BCGen/HBC/BytecodeList.def, MIT
License) using the JSON layout popularized by hbctool (MIT License); both
license texts are included in ios/THIRD_PARTY/.
android/shell/gradle/wrapper/ contains the Gradle Wrapper, and the prebuilt
Android shell includes parts of the Kotlin standard library; both are
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

Original Grok Bot programs
--------------------------

This repository contains no Grok Bot program files. The patch tools download
the official programs on the user's own machine, verify their hashes and patch
them there. Generated clients and web client bundles are not distributed.
Grok, Grok Bot and related names and marks belong to their respective owners.
ProkBot Plus is not affiliated with or endorsed by them.
